NAME
     split - split a file into pieces

SYNOPSIS
     split [-l N] [-b SIZE] [-a N] [-d] [FILE [PREFIX]]

DESCRIPTION
     split writes FILE (or standard input) out in pieces called PREFIX
     followed by a suffix -- aa, ab, ac by default. Without options the
     pieces are a thousand lines each.

OPTIONS
     -l N     N lines per piece
     -b SIZE  SIZE bytes per piece; SIZE may end in K, M or G
     -a N     N letters of suffix
     -d       number the suffixes instead of lettering them

SEE ALSO
     cat(1), head(1), tail(1)
